https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=djU4Lq_5EaM  (Capo 4)

TIP:  The chords in the second verse are sharped.  Either slide the capo up one fret or skip the next verse/chorus and play the one afterwards.  The chords look messy but they're just familiar ones played on different frets.  (A#m) is played like a (Bm) on the 1st fret, (C#) like a (D/A) on the 1st fret, and (G#) like an (F) on the 4th fret.  There's also a "simple" version without sharped chords.


